{{main page image/DYK|image=File:Flag_of_Tamazgha.svg|caption=Flag of Tamazgha}}

* ... that '''[[Tamazgha]]''' uses the Tifinagh script in its native name and is styled as the "Taghlan of Tamazgha," with its capital located at Agadis?

* ... that the '''[[Burawa|Kingdom of Burawa]]''' managed colonies as far afield as Lacashe in Abyala during its medieval imperial era between 1180 and 1516 AD?

* ... that the '''[[Energy Standard Organization]]''' functions as a de facto monetary union that bases its entire financial system on energy production rather than traditional currency?

* ... that the city of '''[[Okami]]''' underwent a distinct historical period known as the Honda Period and features modern infrastructure hubs like Chuo Station?

* ... that '''[[Balisca]]''' is recognized for having some of the world's most progressive LGBTQ rights, with queer culture playing a prominent role in its literature and cinema?

* ... that '''/toju''' is a secretive Baliscan anonymous hacktivist collective that styles its name like a chat command and launches cyberattacks against governments and corporations?

* ... that the '''[[Hoggaanka system]]''' was a formalized governance structure established in 1105 by Marcel II of Burawa to divide rule between centralized areas and delegated administrators?

* ... that planets in the '''[[Aurelius system]]''', such as the ice giant [[Centinela]], now have their own dedicated category on the wiki to document the system's celestial mechanics?
